=== Private universities ===

Private universities include Catholic and secular institutions:

* '''[[Balboan Jesuit University]]''' — A private Catholic university founded in 1903, located in [[La Seu (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|La Seu]], [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]]. Smaller and more selective than the Universitat de Sant Cristòfor, with strengths in philosophy, theology, law, and the liberal arts.

* '''[[Zong University of Sant Cristòfor]]''' — A private university founded in 1912 by the Zong community, located in [[Barri del Te (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Barri del Te]], [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]]. Originally a Zong-language institution, it was reconstituted as a multilingual institution under the Twelve Guarantees' cultural protections and retains Zong and Sinchewese language programmes. It is the principal centre for Fosian studies in Balboa.

* '''[[Escola d'Arts de Barcelona]]''' — A private arts school located in [[Barcelona (ciutat)|Barcelona]], [[Sant Cristòfor]]. The institution is among the most selective private institutions in the country, specialising in visual arts, design, and architecture.

* '''[[Universitat Costa Nord]]''' — A private university located in [[Costa Nord (ciutat)|Costa Nord]], [[Sant Cristòfor]]. An elite institution serving the wealthy residential communities of the Costa Nord coast.

=== Community colleges ===

Community colleges operate in most cities with populations over 100,000, offering two-year associate degrees and vocational certificates. They provide post-secondary vocational training and serve as an alternative pathway to higher education for students who do not pursue or qualify for university admission.

=== Military education ===

The '''[[Acadèmia Militar de Balboa]]''' (Balboa Military Academy) is the principal military training institution in the country, operating three campuses:

* [[Haicang]] — the primary campus, co-located with the naval base on the Aethiopian coast of [[Estret Province|Estret]]
* [[Portblanc]] — a campus in [[Tramuntana Province|Tramuntana]]
* [[Sant Bart]] — a campus in [[Jala Province|Jala]]

The academy trains officers for the Balboan armed forces and operates outside the civilian university system, though its degrees are recognised by the Ministeri d'Educació.

=== International institutions ===

The '''[[University of Huwei]]''', based in [[Huwei]], the capital of [[Zong]], maintains a large satellite campus in [[Sant Cristòfor]]. The campus serves a significant population of international students through a rotation programme in which students alternate between the main campus in Huwei and the Sant Cristòfor campus. It is the largest international university presence in Balboa.

== Outcomes and disparities ==

=== Graduation rates ===

The primary graduation rate is 99 per cent, reflecting near-universal completion of primary education. The secondary graduation rate is 87 per cent overall, with a significant gender gap: approximately 95 per cent for women and 85 per cent for men, a ten-percentage-point disparity favouring women.

=== Geographic disparities ===

Educational attainment varies significantly by province. In [[Estret Province|Estret]], approximately 42 per cent of the adult population has completed post-secondary education; in [[Tramuntana Province|Tramuntana]], the figure is approximately 12 per cent. The geographic disparities reflect broader economic inequalities between the canal corridor and the interior provinces.

=== Ethnic disparities ===

The [[Birú people|Birú]] community has the lowest rates of educational attainment in Balboa, with limited access to secondary and post-secondary education in the remote highland districts. The [[Twelve Guarantees]] include provisions for indigenous cultural protection, but implementation has been limited. The [[Hill Cleaning Programme]] of the 1980s, which addressed the socioeconomic root causes of highland drug manufacturing, provided economic incentives for Birú communities to transition to legitimate tourism and trade, but the educational gap persists.

=== Reparations programme ===

The Twelve Guarantees mandated educational scholarships for descendants of enslaved persons as part of the reparations programme. The [[Balboan Land and Reparations Authority]] administers the scholarship programme alongside land redistribution and cooperative farm support.

